{
  "dom_id": "step-450033",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Computing a 3-Tensor Derivative",
  "problem": "Consider a function $\\mathbf{f}: \\mathbb R^{2\\times 3} \\to \\mathbb R^2$ defined by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14217875/assets/7583605f8c8c3cd07389b8f31c6bfc4eaaf3a6488f226a05d5e0972e5272c2c8.svg)\nGiven that $a_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $\\mathbf{A}$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, find the value of $\\dfrac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial a_{12}}.$",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the function $\\mathbf{f}$ as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14217875/assets/ed6fb0575a19c9afb201170a089841d0271e20e219c54c956e03f5d3e8c87f41.svg)\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f_1}{\\partial a_{12}} = \\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial a_{12}} (-a_{11} + 3a_{12} + 7a_{13} ) = 3.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
